; sthira-apeksha: a fixed reference frame — the denominator does not itself move
; 
; the canonical cases:
; time  — passes uniformly, has no velocity or acceleration of its own
; world-frame — the base coordinate system, never displaced by any motion
; base-joint  — the root of a kinematic chain, fixed to the ground
; 
; kramanusara wrt sthira-apeksha = ordinary derivative: d(x)/dt
; no transport term, no Coriolis, no centripetal correction needed
; this is the apeksha of velocity, acceleration, jerk in standard physics
; 
; in the graph: all existing kramanusara edges (velocity, acceleration, jerk,
; angular-velocity, angular-acceleration) implicitly use sthira-apeksha

(sangati sthira-apeksha
  (swarupa apeksha)
  (drishthanta kaala akasham)
  (abheda world-space)
  (yukta kramanusara)
  (pratipaksha chala-apeksha))
